export default {"id":"sounddesign-level-14","number":14,"title":"Systems Capstone","skillBand":"Textbook","duration":"From the course textbook","summary":"- Master the Macro Architecture of Ableton Live 12 Instrument and Audio Effect Racks (8-16 Macro Knobs, Macro Variations / Snapshot Engine). - Standardize the 8-Macro Universal Layout aligned with Novation Launchkey MK4 physical rotary enco","modules":[{"id":"sounddesign-m-14-1-1","code":"14.1","title":"Macro Systems & Launchkey Mapping","blurb":"- Master the Macro Architecture of Ableton Live 12 Instrument and Audio Effect Racks (8-16 Macro Knobs, Macro Variations / Snapshot Engine). - Standardize the 8-Macro Universal Layout aligned with Novation Launchkey MK4 physical rotary enco","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"sounddesign-l-o-60","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Learning Objectives","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Master the <strong>Macro Architecture</strong> of Ableton Live 12 Instrument and Audio Effect Racks (8-16 Macro Knobs, Macro Variations / Snapshot Engine).","Standardize the <strong>8-Macro Universal Layout</strong> aligned with Novation Launchkey MK4 physical rotary encoders in <strong>Plugin Mode</strong>.","Execute <strong>Multi-Parameter Macro Mapping</strong> (routing one physical knob to simultaneously modulate multiple disparate parameters across inverted and non-linear ranges).","Calibrate parameter minimum/maximum boundaries and inverted response curves.","Build <strong>Macro Variations</strong> (instant snapshot state recall across 4 distinct instrument roles).","Assemble and save the <strong>Universal 8-Macro Master Instrument Template</strong>."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-1-1","title":"14.1.1 — Macro Architecture in Ableton Live 12","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.1.1 — Macro Architecture in Ableton Live 12","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"An Ableton <strong>Macro</strong> is an assignable software control knob located in the header of an Instrument, Audio Effect, or MIDI Effect Rack:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">[ PHYSICAL HARDWARE ENCODER ] ===&gt; [ RACK MACRO 1 ] ===+===&gt; [ PARAMETER A: Filter 1 Cutoff (200 Hz -&gt; 8 kHz) ]\n                                                       +===&gt; [ PARAMETER B: Filter 1 Resonance (0.2 -&gt; 0.7)    ]\n                                                       +===&gt; [ PARAMETER C: Waveshaper Drive (0 dB -&gt; +12 dB)  ]</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Live 12 Capabilities:</strong> Racks can display from <strong>1 to 16 Macro knobs</strong>, featuring color-coding, custom naming, and bidirectional synchronization with hardware controllers."],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Ableton Live 12 Reference Manual</em>, Chapter 24 (Instrument, Drum and Effect Racks)","<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §9"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-1-2","title":"14.1.2 — The 8-Macro Standard for Novation Launchkey MK4","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.1.2 — The 8-Macro Standard for Novation Launchkey MK4","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"To ensure immediate muscle memory and hardware fluency during production, all custom patches designed in this course adhere to the <strong>Universal 8-Macro Hardware Map</strong>:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                        THE UNIVERSAL 8-MACRO HARDWARE BLUEPRINT                                   |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------+\n| HARDWARE ENCODER  | UNIVERSAL MACRO ASSIGNMENT  | OPERATIONAL SOUND DESIGN DOMAIN                 |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------+\n| **Knob 1**        | **Timbre / Brightness**     | Filter Cutoff, FM Amount, Wavetable Morph.      |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------+\n| **Knob 2**        | **Resonance / Formant**     | Filter $Q$, Formant Position, Comb Feedback.    |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------+\n| **Knob 3**        | **Drive / Saturation**      | Waveshaper Drive, Saturator, Tube Bias.         |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------+\n| **Knob 4**        | **Modulation Rate / Speed** | LFO 1 Wobble Sync Rate, Vibrato Speed.          |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------+\n| **Knob 5**        | **Envelope Decay / Shape**  | Filter / Amp Decay Time (Pluck to Sustained).   |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------+\n| **Knob 6**        | **Stereo Width / Chorus**   | Unison Detune Spread, Utility Width, Chorus Mix.|\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------+\n| **Knob 7**        | **Space / Time Echo**       | Delay Ping-Pong Mix &amp; Feedback.                 |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------+\n| **Knob 8**        | **Acoustic Reverb Tail**    | Reverb Size, Decay, and Wet Mix.                |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"Selecting any custom Rack in Live 12 while your Launchkey MK4 is in <strong>Plugin Mode</strong> locks physical encoders 1–8 directly to these controls."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §9","<em>Ableton-Live-12-VST3-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §4"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-1-3","title":"14.1.3 — Multi-Parameter Macro Mapping","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.1.3 — Multi-Parameter Macro Mapping","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"A single Macro knob can control up to dozens of parameters simultaneously across completely different devices inside the rack:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">Turning Macro 1 (\"AGGRESSION\") Clockwise:\n- Filter 1 Cutoff:  Opens UP from 200 Hz to 12 kHz  (Increases brightness)\n- Waveshaper Drive: Increases from +0 dB to +14 dB   (Increases distortion)\n- Master Volume:    Decreases from 0.0 dB to -4.5 dB (Prevents master bus clipping!)</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"This transforms a complex 15-parameter synthesis patch into a single, intuitive performance gesture."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Ableton Live 12 Reference Manual</em>, Chapter 24 (Macro Mapping)"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-1-4","title":"14.1.4 — Macro Scaling and Inverted Ranges","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.1.4 — Macro Scaling and Inverted Ranges","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Clicking the <strong><code>Map</code></strong> button in an Instrument Rack header opens the <strong>Macro Mapping Browser</strong>:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                     MACRO MAPPING BROWSER                                         |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| MACRO KNOB        | TARGET PARAMETER            | MINIMUM VALUE         | MAXIMUM VALUE           |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+\n| **Macro 1**       | Auto Filter Frequency       | $180\\text{ Hz}$       | $9.5\\text{ kHz}$        |\n| **Macro 1**       | Saturator Drive             | $0.0\\text{ dB}$       | $+10.5\\text{ dB}$       |\n| **Macro 1**       | Utility Gain (Inverted!)    | **$+2.0\\text{ dB}$**  | **$-4.0\\text{ dB}$**    |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Inverted Range Mapping:</strong> Setting Minimum to +2 dB and Maximum to -4 dB causes the parameter to <em>decrease</em> as you turn the knob clockwise, creating automatic gain compensation."],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Ableton Live 12 Reference Manual</em>, Chapter 24 (Mapping Dialog)"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-1-5","title":"14.1.5 — Macro Variations: Snapshot States","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.1.5 — Macro Variations: Snapshot States","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ableton Live 12 features <strong>Macro Variations</strong>, allowing you to capture and store complete snapshots of all Macro knob positions:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">[ INSTRUMENT RACK: \"SD_Lead_Master_System\" ]\n  |\n  +---&gt; [ SNAPSHOT 1: \"Warm Rhodes Key\"  ] (Cutoff: Low, Drive: Zero, Reverb: 15%)\n  +---&gt; [ SNAPSHOT 2: \"Punchy FM Pluck\"   ] (Cutoff: Med, Mod Decay: 120ms, Drive: +3dB)\n  +---&gt; [ SNAPSHOT 3: \"Screaming Acid Lead\"] (Cutoff: High, Res: 85%, Drive: +12dB)\n  +---&gt; [ SNAPSHOT 4: \"Ethereal Cloud Pad\"] (Cutoff: Med, Attack: 2s, Reverb: 50%)</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["Click the <strong>Camera Icon</strong> in the Rack header to open the Variations panel.","Dial in your Macro knobs for a specific sound and click <strong><code>New</code></strong>.","Live stores that state as Snapshot 1.","Dial in a completely different sound state and save Snapshot 2.","Clicking the <strong>Play ()</strong> icon beside any snapshot instantly morphs the entire synth engine into that exact sonic state."],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Ableton Live 12 Reference Manual</em>, Chapter 24 (Macro Variations)"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-1-6","title":"14.1.6 — Building the Universal 8-Macro Master Template","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.1.6 — Building the Universal 8-Macro Master Template","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">1. INSERT EMPTY INSTRUMENT RACK ON A MIDI TRACK.\n2. NAME THE 8 MACROS EXACTLY:\n   [1: Timbre] [2: Res/Form] [3: Drive] [4: Mod Rate]\n   [5: Decay]  [6: Width]    [7: Delay] [8: Space]\n3. RIGHT-CLICK RACK HEADER -&gt; \"Save as Default Preset\".</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"Now, every time you group a synthesizer in Live 12, your universal 8-macro template is instantiated automatically."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §9"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"sounddesign-m-14-2-2","code":"14.2","title":"Preset Architecture & Library Discipline","blurb":"- Architect and maintain a professional Sound Design Preset Library inside Ableton Live 12's User Library. - Implement the strict Universal Naming Convention: SD_[Engine]_[Category]_[Descriptor].","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"sounddesign-l-o-61","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Learning Objectives","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Architect and maintain a professional <strong>Sound Design Preset Library</strong> inside Ableton Live 12's <strong>User Library</strong>.","Implement the strict <strong>Universal Naming Convention</strong>: <code>SD_[Engine]_[Category]_[Descriptor]</code>.","Leverage the <strong>Live 12 Tagging &amp; Similarity System</strong> (Categorical, Timbral, and Character metadata tags).","Structure categorical storage directories across 8 universal instrument roles.","Export, archive, and back up native <code>.adv</code> (device) and <code>.adg</code> (rack) preset files.","Enforce the professional <strong>60-Second Archive Discipline</strong>."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-2-1","title":"14.2.1 — The Sound Designer's User Library Architecture","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.2.1 — The Sound Designer's User Library Architecture","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"A professional sound designer's primary career asset is their personal preset archive. "},{"type":"prose","html":"Inside Ableton Live 12, navigate to <strong><code>User Library</code> → <code>Presets</code> → <code>Instruments</code></strong> and construct the following folder structure:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">[ USER LIBRARY / PRESETS / INSTRUMENTS / SOUND DESIGN MASTER LIBRARY ]\n  |\n  +---&gt; 01_Sub_Basses/        (Clean sines, 808s, rolling subs)\n  +---&gt; 02_Mid_Basses/        (Reeses, wubs, growls, neuro stabs)\n  +---&gt; 03_Plucks/            (House FM plucks, kawaii bells, kotos)\n  +---&gt; 04_Leads/             (Supersaws, glide monos, screech leads)\n  +---&gt; 05_Pads_Atmospheres/  (Wavetable pads, granular choirs, drone beds)\n  +---&gt; 06_Chord_Stabs/       (Organ stabs, minor 9th vinyl chops)\n  +---&gt; 07_Synth_Drums/       (Synthetic kicks, snares, hats, percs)\n  +---&gt; 08_Sound_Effects/     (Noise risers, laser drops, downlifters)</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Ableton Live 12 Reference Manual</em>, Chapter 5 (Managing Files and Sets)","<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §16"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-2-2","title":"14.2.2 — The Universal Preset Naming Convention","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.2.2 — The Universal Preset Naming Convention","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Every custom patch created in your studio must follow the standardized four-token syntax:"},{"type":"prose","html":"SD\\_[Engine]\\_[Category]\\_[Descriptor]"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                               PRESET NAMING SYNTAX EXAMPLES                                       |\n+--------------------------+-----------------------+------------------------------------------------+\n| FILE NAME                | SYNTHESIS ENGINE      | INSTRUMENT DESCRIPTION                         |\n+--------------------------+-----------------------+------------------------------------------------+\n| `SD_Op_Bass_DonkHouse`   | `Ableton Operator`    | 1:2 FM Donk Bass for Deep House.               |\n| `SD_Vit_Growl_FormantYoi`| `Vital`               | Vocal Formant Dubstep Growl.                   |\n| `SD_Sur_Reese_1995Roll`  | `Surge XT`            | 20-Cent Detuned Drum &amp; Bass Reese.             |\n| `SD_Drf_Lead_Acid303`    | `Ableton Drift`       | Saturated 303 Resonant Acid Bass.              |\n| `SD_Vit_Chord_Supersaw32`| `Vital`               | 32-Voice Euphoric Future Bass Chord Stack.     |\n| `SD_Op_Perc_808Cowbell`  | `Ableton Operator`    | Fixed-Frequency Inharmonic Cowbell.            |\n| `SD_Rck_Hybrid_PluckSub` | `Instrument Rack`     | Multi-Engine Layered Pluck and Clean Sub.      |\n+--------------------------+-----------------------+------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §16"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-2-3","title":"14.2.3 — Live 12 Tagging & Similarity Metadata","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.2.3 — Live 12 Tagging & Similarity Metadata","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Live 12 introduces a global <strong>Metadata Tagging System</strong>:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">[ PRESET FILE ] ===&gt; Right-Click -&gt; \"Edit Tags\"\n                           |\n                           +---&gt; Sound Category:  [ Bass ]\n                           +---&gt; Timbre Tag:      [ Metallic, Saturated, Bouncy ]\n                           +---&gt; Genre / Mood:    [ UK Garage, Dark ]</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["Tagging your custom presets allows Live 12's <strong>Sound Similarity Search</strong> engine to instantly suggest your custom patches whenever you search for matching sonic characteristics."],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Ableton Live 12 Reference Manual</em>, Chapter 5 (Tagging and Searching)"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-2-4","title":"14.2.4 — Categorical Storage Structure","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.2.4 — Categorical Storage Structure","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Organize your library by <strong>Musical Role</strong> rather than by plugin brand:"},{"type":"list","items":["Placing all basses in <code>01_Sub_Basses</code> and <code>02_Mid_Basses</code> (regardless of whether they were built in Operator, Vital, or Surge XT) ensures that when you need a bass during a songwriting session, you find all options in one folder without menu-diving."],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Ultimate Sound Design: Mastering Sound Design</em>, Section 13.1"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-2-5","title":"14.2.5 — Exporting and Backing Up Sound Libraries","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.2.5 — Exporting and Backing Up Sound Libraries","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ableton saves individual instrument presets as <strong><code>.adv</code></strong> files (Ableton Device Preset) and instrument racks as <strong><code>.adg</code></strong> files (Ableton Device Group):"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Preset Files:</strong> All stored in <code>C:\\Users\\<you>\\Documents\\Ableton\\User Library\\Presets\\</code>.","<strong>Cloud / External Backup:</strong> Regularly back up your <code>User Library/Presets</code> directory to external storage (<code>B:\\Documents\\</code>).","<strong>Preset Self-Containment:</strong> When saving an Instrument Rack containing samples (in <code>Simpler</code>), right-click the Rack and select <strong>Collect All and Save</strong> to ensure all associated audio files are bundled inside the preset folder."],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Ableton Live 12 Reference Manual</em>, Chapter 5"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-2-6","title":"14.2.6 — The 60-Second Archive Discipline","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.2.6 — The 60-Second Archive Discipline","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">THE LAW OF THE SOUND DESIGNER:\n\"Whenever you create an exceptional, unique sound during any production session,\nyou MUST pause for 60 seconds, name the rack using the SD_ syntax, map its 8 macros,\nand drag it into your User Library before moving on.\"</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"Following this discipline guarantees that within six months, you will possess a bespoke, personal library of over 100 signature, production-ready instruments that exist nowhere else in the world."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound-Design-Beginner-Knowledgebase.md</em>, §16","<em>Ultimate Sound Design: Mastering Sound Design</em>, Section 13.2"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"sounddesign-m-14-3-3","code":"14.3","title":"Final Capstone Exam (The 10-Patch Master Exam)","blurb":"- Execute the comprehensive 10-Patch Master Sound Design Exam under strict laboratory examination conditions. - Synthesize ten production-grade instruments completely from an initialized (init) state with zero external presets across Ableto","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"sounddesign-l-o-62","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Learning Objectives","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Execute the comprehensive <strong>10-Patch Master Sound Design Exam</strong> under strict laboratory examination conditions.","Synthesize ten production-grade instruments completely from an initialized (<code>init</code>) state with zero external presets across <strong>Ableton Operator</strong>, <strong>Vital</strong>, <strong>Surge XT</strong>, <strong>Drift</strong>, and <strong>Instrument Racks</strong>:","<code>SD_Op_Exam_808GlidingSub</code>","<code>SD_Sur_Exam_ModernReese</code>","<code>SD_Op_Exam_ClassicFMPluck</code>","<code>SD_Vit_Exam_FormantGrowl</code>","<code>SD_Vit_Exam_EuphoricSupersaw</code>","<code>SD_Drf_Exam_Acid303Squelch</code>","<code>SD_Sur_Exam_KarplusStringPluck</code>","<code>SD_Vit_Exam_Evolving3DPad</code>","<code>SD_Op_Exam_SyntheticDrumKit</code>","<code>SD_Rck_Exam_MultiEngineMasterLayer</code>","Verify each patch against rigorous <strong>Acoustic &amp; Technical Rubric Standards</strong> (Gain Staging, Phase Coherence, Headroom, Frequency Separation, Macro Mapping).","Complete <strong>Gate K: Final Graduation Checkpoint</strong> and ratify the <strong>Sound Designer's Credo</strong>."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-3-1","title":"14.3.1 — Capstone Exam Overview & Evaluation Rubric","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.3.1 — Capstone Exam Overview & Evaluation Rubric","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"The <strong>10-Patch Capstone Exam</strong> evaluates your ability to construct professional, club-ready sounds entirely from scratch without relying on presets, sample packs, or guessing."},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                CAPSTONE EXAMINATION RUBRIC                                        |\n+-------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| EVALUATION DOMAIN | PASSING CRITERIA SPECIFICATION                                                |\n+-------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **1. Init Discipline**| Every patch MUST begin from a verified initialized template (`Init`).     |\n+-------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **2. Gain Staging**| All patches must peak at **$-6.0\\text{ dBFS} \\pm 1.0\\text{ dB}$** with zero  |\n|                   | digital clipping or inter-sample distortion.                                  |\n+-------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **3. Phase / Mono**| Sub-bass frequencies ($&lt;120\\text{ Hz}$) must be $100\\%$ phase-coherent &amp; mono.|\n+-------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **4. Macro System**| All 8 Macros mapped to the Universal Hardware Map for Launchkey MK4 Plugin.  |\n+-------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| **5. Archive Spec**| All patches saved with `SD_[Engine]_[Category]_[Descriptor]` naming syntax.   |\n+-------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-3-2","title":"14.3.2 — Exam Patch 1: The Gliding 808 Trap Sub","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.3.2 — Exam Patch 1: The Gliding 808 Trap Sub","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| EXAM PATCH 1: `SD_Op_Exam_808GlidingSub`                                      |\n+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Engine**           | **Ableton Operator** (Algorithm 11)                    |\n| **Core Oscillator**  | Sine Wave, Coarse: **0.5**, Retrigger: **ON (0 deg)**  |\n| **Pitch Envelope**   | Amount: **+24 st**, Decay: **22 ms** (Punchy thud)     |\n| **Saturator / Drive**| `Saturator` (Soft Sine: +3 dB) -&gt; `Erosion` (Sine: 4 kHz)|\n| **Voicing**          | **Mono Legato**, Glide Time: **110 ms**                |\n| **Output Metering**  | Peak: **-6.0 dBFS**, `Utility` Bass Mono @ 120 Hz      |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-3-3","title":"14.3.3 — Exam Patch 2: Modern Neuro Reese Bass","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.3.3 — Exam Patch 2: Modern Neuro Reese Bass","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| EXAM PATCH 2: `SD_Sur_Exam_ModernReese`                                       |\n+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Engine**           | **Surge XT** (Classic Engine)                          |\n| **Oscillators**      | Osc 1: Saw (-10 cents); Osc 2: Saw (+10 cents) (20c beat)|\n| **Filter Matrix**    | **Serial 2 Routing:** Filter 1 (Ladder LP24 @ 380 Hz)  |\n|                      | -&gt; Waveshaper (Soft Clip +6 dB) -&gt; Filter 2 (HP @ 35Hz)|\n| **Sub Isolation**    | Osc 3: Pure Sine Sub (-2 Oct, Mono Direct)             |\n| **Modulation**       | Voice LFO 1 (1/4th Sync) -&gt; Filter 1 Cutoff (+25%)     |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-3-4","title":"14.3.4 — Exam Patch 3: Classic Deep House FM Pluck","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.3.4 — Exam Patch 3: Classic Deep House FM Pluck","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| EXAM PATCH 3: `SD_Op_Exam_ClassicFMPluck`                                     |\n+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Engine**           | **Ableton Operator** (Algorithm 1)                     |\n| **Operator A (Car)** | Sine, Coarse: **1**, Level: **0.0 dB**, Decay: **280 ms**|\n| **Operator B (Mod)** | Sine, Coarse: **2**, Level: **-12.0 dB**, Decay: **120 ms**|\n| **Subtractive Filter**| **Bypassed** (Pure 1:2 Phase Modulation sidebands)     |\n| **Voicing**          | Polyphony: **6 Voices**                                |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-3-5","title":"14.3.5 — Exam Patch 4: Vocal Formant Dubstep Growl","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.3.5 — Exam Patch 4: Vocal Formant Dubstep Growl","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| EXAM PATCH 4: `SD_Vit_Exam_FormantGrowl`                                      |\n+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Engine**           | **Vital**                                              |\n| **Oscillator 1**     | Basic Shapes (Saw), Warp: **Formant Scale (Warp @ 25%)**|\n| **Filter 1**         | Mode: **Dirty LP24**, Cutoff: **220 Hz**, Drive: **+4 dB**|\n| **Modulation**       | LFO 1 (1/4th Trigger) -&gt; Formant Scale (+65%) &amp; Cutoff (+60%)|\n| **Effects Rack**     | 1. Distortion (Soft Clip +12 dB) -&gt; 2. Multiband (OTT 75%)|\n| **Voicing**          | **Mono**                                               |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-3-6","title":"14.3.6 — Exam Patch 5: 32-Voice Euphoric Supersaw","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.3.6 — Exam Patch 5: 32-Voice Euphoric Supersaw","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| EXAM PATCH 5: `SD_Vit_Exam_EuphoricSupersaw`                                  |\n+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Engine**           | **Vital**                                              |\n| **Oscillators**      | Osc 1: Saw (16 Voices, 24% Detune, 100% Spread)        |\n|                      | Osc 2: Saw (+1 Oct, 12 Voices, 18% Detune, Level -4dB) |\n|                      | Osc 3: Square (-1 Oct, 4 Voices, Level -6dB)           |\n| **Pitch Scoop**      | Envelope 2 (+12 st, Decay 50 ms) -&gt; Osc 1 &amp; 2 Pitch    |\n| **Effects Rack**     | Multiband Compressor (60%) -&gt; Chorus (25%) -&gt; Reverb (20%)|\n| **Voicing**          | Polyphony: **8 Voices**                                |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-3-7","title":"14.3.7 — Exam Patch 6: Resonant Acid 303 Bass","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.3.7 — Exam Patch 6: Resonant Acid 303 Bass","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| EXAM PATCH 6: `SD_Drf_Exam_Acid303Squelch`                                    |\n+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Engine**           | **Ableton Drift**                                      |\n| **Oscillator 1**     | Sawtooth, Octave: **-1**                               |\n| **Filter**           | Low-Pass LP24 (Saturated), Cutoff: **220 Hz**, Res: **0.84**|\n| **Filter Envelope**  | Attack: **0 ms**, Decay: **130 ms**, Depth: **+75%**   |\n| **Downstream FX**    | `Overdrive` (Drive +5 dB) -&gt; `Delay` (1/16th Dotted)   |\n| **Voicing**          | **Mono Legato**, Glide Time: **55 ms**                 |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-3-8","title":"14.3.8 — Exam Patch 7: Karplus-Strong Physical Pluck","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.3.8 — Exam Patch 7: Karplus-Strong Physical Pluck","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| EXAM PATCH 7: `SD_Sur_Exam_KarplusStringPluck`                                |\n+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Engine**           | **Surge XT**                                           |\n| **Oscillator 1**     | Algorithm: **String**, Damping: **0.30**, Decay: **2.5 s**|\n| **Filter 1**         | Low-Pass LP12, Cutoff: **8.0 kHz**                     |\n| **Effects Bus**      | Airwindows Galactic Reverb (Mix: 25%) -&gt; Delay (Mix: 15%)|\n| **Voicing**          | Polyphony: **8 Voices** (Velocity sensitive dynamics)  |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-3-9","title":"14.3.9 — Exam Patch 8: Evolving 3D Wavetable Ambient Pad","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.3.9 — Exam Patch 8: Evolving 3D Wavetable Ambient Pad","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| EXAM PATCH 8: `SD_Vit_Exam_Evolving3DPad`                                     |\n+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Engine**           | **Vital**                                              |\n| **Oscillator 1**     | Vocal Formants, Unison: 4 Voices, Warp: Vocode (30%)   |\n| **Oscillator 2**     | Glass / Shimmer, Octave: +1, Warp: Inharmonic Smear    |\n| **Modulation**       | LFO 1 (Free 0.08 Hz) -&gt; Wavetable Position 1 &amp; 2 (+70%)|\n| **Envelopes**        | AEG 1: Attack **1.8 s**, Sustain **90%**, Release **3.0 s**|\n| **Effects Rack**     | Reverb (Size 85%, Decay 4.5 s, Low Cut 280 Hz, Mix 35%)|\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-3-10","title":"14.3.10 — Exam Patch 9: Synthetic Electronic Drum Kit","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.3.10 — Exam Patch 9: Synthetic Electronic Drum Kit","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| EXAM PATCH 9: `SD_Op_Exam_SyntheticDrumKit` (Drum Rack with 4 Operator Pads)  |\n+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Pad 1 (C1: Kick)** | Operator: Sine Body + Fixed Click (1.4 kHz) + Pitch Env|\n| **Pad 2 (D1: Snare)**| Operator: 180 Hz Body + Fixed Noise Wires (8.5 kHz)    |\n| **Pad 3 (F#1: Hat)** | Operator: Fixed Inharmonic Square/Sine Metal + HP24    |\n| **Pad 4 (G#1: Perc)**| Operator: 808 Cowbell (Dual Inharmonic Fixed Freqs)    |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-3-11","title":"14.3.11 — Exam Patch 10: Multi-Engine Layered Master Instrument","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.3.11 — Exam Patch 10: Multi-Engine Layered Master Instrument","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| EXAM PATCH 10: `SD_Rck_Exam_MultiEngineMasterLayer` (Ableton Instrument Rack) |\n+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------------+\n| **Chain 1: SUB**     | `Drift` (Pure Sine, Mono, EQ Eight LP48 @ 100 Hz)      |\n| **Chain 2: MID**     | `Vital` (16-Voice Supersaw, EQ Eight BP 100Hz-3kHz)    |\n| **Chain 3: TOP**     | `Collision` (Wood Mallet Click, EQ Eight HP48 @ 3 kHz) |\n| **Master Macros**    | All 8 Universal Macros Mapped and Verified             |\n| **Master Metering**  | Peak: **-6.0 dBFS**, Zero Clipping                     |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"sounddesign-l-14-3-12","title":"14.3.12 — Gate K: Final Graduation Checkpoint & The Sound Designer's Credo","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"14.3.12 — Gate K: Final Graduation Checkpoint & The Sound Designer's Credo","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                             GATE K FINAL CHECKLIST                            |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| [ ] 1. All 10 Exam Patches synthesized from an initialized (`init`) state.    |\n| [ ] 2. All 10 Patches verified on Spectrum for frequency separation.          |\n| [ ] 3. Sub-basses confirmed 100% mono and phase-coherent via Utility.         |\n| [ ] 4. All 8 Universal Macros mapped and verified on Launchkey MK4.           |\n| [ ] 5. All 10 Presets archived in User Library with `SD_` syntax.             |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">=================================================================================\n                          THE SOUND DESIGNER'S CREDO\n=================================================================================\n1. I do not browse presets looking for inspiration; I hear sound first in my mind \n   and synthesize it with purpose.\n2. I honor the fundamental physics of sound: frequency, amplitude, and phase.\n3. I keep my sub-bass pure, mono, and anchored beneath my midrange timbres.\n4. I use distortion to generate new harmonic overtones and filters to sculpt them.\n5. I modulate with intention: rate, depth, shape, and destination.\n6. I protect dynamic headroom: peaking at -6 dBFS and respecting dry presence.\n7. I master my tools: Operator, Surge XT, Vital, Drift, and Ableton Live 12.\n8. I am a master sound designer.\n=================================================================================</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>CONGRATULATIONS. YOU HAVE COMPLETED SOUND DESIGN FOUNDATIONS.</strong>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<em>Sound Design Foundations Syllabus</em>, §3 (Gate K Definition) &amp; §7"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]}]};
